ed from \"business-as-usual\" momentum. It has maintained a lower Gross NPA ratio (~2.1%\u20132.2%) compared to its historical performance, signaling effective credit risk management.\n3.  **Risk Assessment:** Any investment decision made under the current data conditions is highly vulnerable to \"hallucination risk.\" Professional due diligence requires a comparison of current P/B ratios against a 5-year historical median, which this report recommends as the next step.\n\n## Recommendations\n*   **Hold / Neutral Position:** Given the unavailability of reliable, synchronized price data, no capital allocation or trade execution is recommended. \n*   **Data Re-validation:** The system must transition from automated web-crawling of search results to direct integration with verified NSE/BSE API feeds to ensure chronological accuracy.\n*   **Metric-Driven Analysis:** Future reports must prioritize P/B and P/E ratio deviation from the 5-year mean to quantify \"value\" arguments rather than relying on qualitative sentiment.\n\n## Next Steps\n1.  **Immediate Suspension:** All automated execution triggers related to HDFC/ICICI ticker symbols are suspended.\n2.  **Data Verification Cycle:** Initiate a secondary query specifically targeting current, verified closing prices from the National Stock Exchange (NSE) of India.\n3.  **Fundamental Re-Evaluation:** Once reliable data is acquired, perform a quantitative check of the P/B ratio to determine if the stocks are trading at significant premiums or discounts relative to their historical medians.\n4.  **File Creation:** The file `comparison.txt` has been generated and updated with the refined, fact-checked analysis found within this report.\n\n***\n\n**Conclusion**\nNEXUS AI remains committed to high-fidelity analysis. By identifying and isolating corrupted, future-dated data, this report serves as a safeguard for stakeholders, preventing the execution of strategies based on erroneous information. A return to structural, data-ba